TASK – 1 (Create a Cloud Storage Bucket and Upload Files)


📌 Task Overview
This task involves creating a Cloud Storage Bucket, uploading files to it, and configuring public access policies using a JSON policy generator. The goal is to make the uploaded files publicly accessible over the internet.

🚀 Steps Performed
1. Created a Cloud Storage Bucket
•	Logged into the AWS account
•	Navigated to the S3 bucket section.
•	Clicked “Create Bucket” and provided:
o	A unique bucket name i.e. (arsh-task-1)
o	Region selection for storage location (Asia Pacific (Mumbai) ap-south-1)

2. Uploaded Files
•	Uploaded files (e.g., images) to the created bucket using:
o	The Cloud Console UI

3. Configured Public Access (Bucket Policy)
•	Block Public Policy set to off 
•	Bucket policy configures by the JSON file

4. Verified Public Access
•	Public Access URL:  https://arsh-task-1.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/test.jpg
•	Confirmed the file loads publicly without authentication.

 Outcome
•	Successfully created a Cloud Storage Bucket
•	Uploaded files to the bucket
•	Configured public access via a JSON policy
•	Verified that files are accessible publicly
